From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse <build@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:53:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/20] hwcomposer: refuse LINEAR for formats the compositor
 imports through NVIDIA EGL

What: dmabuf_modifiers() records, under formats_mutex, every format for which
the compositor advertises an NVIDIA-vendor (0x03) modifier
(display->nvidia_modifier_formats). compositor_supports() then reports
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR as unsupported for exactly those formats, so the
prepare-time gate (waydroid_mode_impl.h, displayable_buffer) routes such a
layer to SurfaceFlinger composition and the set-time backstop never attaches
it.

Why: NVIDIA's EGL imports a LINEAR dma-buf only as GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES
(external_only = TRUE; measured here 2026-10-11 with a stock GBM + glvnd host
test: LINEAR 2D and renderbuffer binds fail with GL_INVALID_OPERATION,
EXTERNAL_OES works). A compositor that samples client buffers as
GL_TEXTURE_2D but still advertises LINEAR (Mutter/Cogl) fails the import with
zwp_linux_buffer_params error 7, which is fatal to the Wayland connection
(waydroid-nvidia #11).

Source: QuinOvaX, quinovax/waydroid-nvidia main f2c2f39
  (compositor_uses_nvidia_egl() in patches/hwcomposer/0001-wip-nvidia-fixes.patch)
  https://github.com/quinovax/waydroid-nvidia/commit/f2c2f39
  It replaces PR #20 b9f9421 (The-JimmyDev), which refused LINEAR on every
  compositor and so broke the hybrid iGPU present path.
Licence: Apache-2.0 (android_hardware_waydroid; the fork's patches/hwcomposer/
inherit it, waydroid-nvidia LICENSE section 2).

Deviations from the source:
- Per format instead of global. KWin 6.7.5 on NVIDIA (this host) advertises
  LINEAR only for P010, NV12 and XYUV, and for those formats LINEAR is the only
  modifier; every RGB format lists only NVIDIA block-linear modifiers
  (waydroid.modifiers.* properties, 519 entries). The global gate would refuse
  NV12 LINEAR video buffers that KWin explicitly accepts and push every video
  frame through SurfaceFlinger. Hybrid iGPU compositors list no NVIDIA
  modifier, so LINEAR stays allowed there (unchanged from the source).
- No once-computed, unlocked `static int cached`: the source computed the
  answer on first call and kept it forever, so a call before the compositor's
  modifier events arrived cached "not NVIDIA" for the life of the process, and
  it read display->modifiers without a lock. Here the writer maintains the set
  under formats_mutex and the reader consults it under the same lock: no
  cache, no ordering dependency.

Measured 2026-10-12:
- KWin 6.7.5: no decision changes (LINEAR is never listed for a format that
  also has NVIDIA modifiers). Gallery video, launcher, Settings, recents,
  games render as before.
- cage 0.3.1 / wlroots 0.20.2 (nested): lists LINEAR next to NVIDIA modifiers
  for RGB formats, so the gate is active. The gate routes the Gallery video's
  RGB565 LINEAR buffers (usage 0x920) to SurfaceFlinger (CLIENT). Without the
  gate (A/B with the unpatched build) wlroots imports and shows them
  correctly as a DEVICE layer. So on wlroots the gate is conservative and
  costs a GPU composition pass for such layers; it is needed where the
  import fails (Mutter, waydroid-nvidia #11; Mutter not available here,
  not measured).
---
 hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp     |  2 ++
 hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h       |  4 ++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp b/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
index f1fbdc9..ccb6699 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/gralloc_handler.cpp
@@ -170,6 +170,22 @@ bool compositor_supports(display *display, uint32_t drm_format, uint64_t modifie
         return false;
     /* Search under the lock: the Wayland thread may reallocate this vector at any time. */
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(display->formats_mutex);
+    /* NVIDIA's EGL imports a LINEAR dma-buf only as GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES (eglQueryDmaBuf-
+     * ModifiersEXT external_only = TRUE). A compositor that also lists NVIDIA block-linear
+     * modifiers for this format imports it through NVIDIA's EGL, and if it samples client
+     * buffers as GL_TEXTURE_2D (Mutter/Cogl) an advertised LINEAR is a fatal
+     * zwp_linux_buffer_params error 7 ("Could not bind the given EGLImage to a
+     * CoglTexture2D", waydroid-nvidia #11). So LINEAR is refused for such a format and the
+     * layer is composed by SurfaceFlinger instead. Per format, not global: KWin on NVIDIA lists
+     * LINEAR only for YUV formats that have no NVIDIA modifier (it handles those as external
+     * textures), and hybrid iGPU compositors list no NVIDIA modifiers, so both keep LINEAR. */
+    if (modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR && display->nvidia_modifier_formats.count(drm_format)) {
+        static std::atomic<bool> logged{false};
+        if (!logged.exchange(true))
+            ALOGI("compositor imports format 0x%x through NVIDIA EGL; LINEAR buffers of such "
+                  "formats are composed by SurfaceFlinger", drm_format);
+        return false;
+    }
     auto it = display->modifiers.find(drm_format);
     if (it == display->modifiers.end())
         return false;
diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
index 4ef5150..b9e7421 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
@@ -1812,6 +1812,8 @@ dmabuf_modifiers(void *data, struct zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 * dmabuf,
         std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(d->formats_mutex);
         index = d->modifiers[format].size();
         d->modifiers[format].push_back(modifier);
+        if (fourcc_mod_get_vendor(modifier) == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_VENDOR_NVIDIA)
+            d->nvidia_modifier_formats.insert(format);
     }
 
     std::stringstream prop_name_stream;
diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
index 6f5a83f..cb85528 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
@@ -434,6 +434,10 @@ struct display {
      * Every access holds formats_mutex; readers copy what they need out under it. */
     std::mutex formats_mutex;
     std::unordered_set<uint32_t> formats;
+    /* Formats for which the compositor advertised at least one NVIDIA-vendor (0x03) modifier,
+     * i.e. it imports them through NVIDIA's EGL. Maintained by dmabuf_modifiers() under
+     * formats_mutex; see compositor_supports(). */
+    std::unordered_set<uint32_t> nvidia_modifier_formats;
 
     std::map<uint32_t, std::vector<uint64_t>> modifiers;
     std::map<uint32_t, std::string> layer_names;
